The NADAC gap is calculated by subtracting the brand-name NADAC per unit from the corresponding generic NADAC per unit. The proportional gap is calculated by dividing the NADAC gap by the brand-name NADAC per unit. One thing we can immediately notice is that, for most drugs in this comparison, the generic has a lower NADAC per unit than its brand-name counterpart. However, we can also see that there are some drugs for which the generic has a higher NADAC per unit than the brand-name counterpart.

